{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
  "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 09-1533, DePierre v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, the only way to give different meaning to two distinct terms that Congress used in the statute -- \"cocaine\" on the one hand and \"cocaine base\" on the other -- is to make clear that cocaine base means something different than all substances with the chemical formula C17H21NO4."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Pincus, if -- if I understand your interpretation correctly, it would exclude freebase. How is that a sensible interpretation of the statute, one that would exclude freebase, a commonly known substance? Congress was aware of it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If we agree with you, how should a judge instruct a jury to determine whether a substance is crack? Should the judge use the definition in the sentencing guidelines?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you get cocaine into a rock form without using a base? Is there some way that the rock type form of cocaine could ever be achieved without a use of a base?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the way that crack is produced is that cocaine powder is turned back, using the process we've been talking about, into chemically cocaine in this rock-like form."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this were a trial court and we had two world-class chemists, strictly from a chemical standpoint wouldn't they tell you that the cocaine in a leaf is in a salt form, not a base form?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: That is how Congress wrote the statute, though. It defined a large amount of substances and then it pulled out one substance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is it -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But you define it in your brief, and this is very interesting to me -- you talk about it being a yellow substance that came directly from grinding up leaves, something like that. You have the definition there. It's written."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "afb4742b496cd9668317a8374d9ed52e882f103e92be3d6cfc80c99f956f8d82",
      "evidence_id": "ev-afb4742b496c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: It is the case that the paste, just like the freebase and the crack, can be smoked, and for that reason is seen as more addictive than the powder."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1533",
      "confidence": 0.0,
